<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jabalpur</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jubbulpore</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jabalpur is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narmada-river">Narmada</a> river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Nearby Tewar was the site of Tripuri, the capital of the Kalachuris, and later the region formed the heart of the Gond kingdom of Garha. Under British rule, as Jubbulpore, it became a military and administrative centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-provinces">Central Provinces</a>, and today it is one of the largest cities in Madhya Pradesh.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jabalpur.jpg" alt="Jabalpur" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ms Sarah Welch · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:0010322_Chausath_Yogini_Temple_and_Gowri_Shankar_Temple,_Bhedaghat_Madhya_Pradesh_054.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
